{"id":"423449068","kind":"article","title":"测试效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2021-10-20","updated":"2026-10-28","votes":37,"comment_count":4,"minutes":10,"chars":4747,"keywords":["测试效应","检索练习","间隔重复","长期记忆","生成效应","概念学习"],"summary":"词条介绍提取练习的测试效应：尝试从记忆中回忆信息，即使没有立即给出答案，也往往比重复阅读更利于长期保持；生成式测试通常效果更强，且测试效应不等同于生成效应。页面同时列出相关研究，说明间隔重复与提取练习的联系及其对概念学习的可能应用。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/423449068","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"与其他学习活动对比"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"格式"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-4","level":3,"title":"综述"},{"id":"sec-5","level":3,"title":"评论"},{"id":"sec-6","level":3,"title":"一手研究"},{"id":"sec-7","level":2,"title":"反向链接"},{"id":"sec-8","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-9","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"EHe0-JRn\">如果你努力回忆某个细节，那么这个行为本身会强化对细节的记忆。在学习上这么做时，被称作「提取练习」。</p><p data-pid=\"E2A-le3p\">实验证明，即使在没有提供正确答案的情况下，甚至在给予应试者「开卷」以寻找正确答案的情况下，也会产生这种效应。这种效应已经在许多领域和许多年龄段上得到了证明。</p><p data-pid=\"mjj466Mk\">这表明测试的作用明显不同。在典型的课堂上，教师和学生都认为学习是发生在讲课过程中，或在阅读材料时。测试是用来评估学习的。但事实上，测试本身就是学习过程中的一个重要部分。</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">与其他学习活动对比</h2><p data-pid=\"e0l2pbss\">尽管学生在练习过程中的成功率较低，但提取练习比单纯通过重复阅读学习材料能带来更持久的长期记忆 (Roediger, 2006)。相关文章：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z49u8mtc9wZoY7siV7nz4V3PG2oMkNBn7AgUk\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">合意困难（术语来自 Bjork）</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"dslUKMWt\">总体而言，单与基于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的练习相比，测试效应似乎还能带来更持久的记忆 (Karpicke and Smith, 2012)，并改善学习表现 (Karpicke and Blunt, 2011)。</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">格式</h2><p data-pid=\"YoFDpyL6\">一般来说，测试效应在生成式测试（简答题、作文）中比在判别式测试（多选题 / 判断题）中更明显 (例如 Kang et al, 2007)。这可能是由于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>。</p><hr/><h2 id=\"sec-3\">参考文献</h2><h3 id=\"sec-4\">综述</h3><p data-pid=\"YWdc-B2h\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Roediger,_H._L.,_&amp;_Karpicke,_J._D._(2006)._The_Power_of_Testing_Memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Basic Research and Implications for Educational Practice. Perspectives on Psychological Science, 1(3), 181–210.</a></p><p data-pid=\"cUCgj8H5\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Pan,_S._C.,_&amp;_Rickard,_T._C._(2018)._Transfer_of_test-enhanced_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Meta-analytic review and synthesis. Psychological Bulletin, 144(7), 710–756</a>, 特别聚焦于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2a8QGPfUmdLCVokLaegNzmaU6ehC58CUtYi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">提取练习和迁移学习</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup></p><p data-pid=\"GpXpZKEd\">Branwen, G. (2009). 高效学习的间隔重复<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>。2019 年 12 月 16 日检索，来自 <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://www.gwern.net/Spaced-repetition\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://www.</span><span class=\"visible\">gwern.net/Spaced-repeti</span><span class=\"invisible\">tion</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a></p><h3 id=\"sec-5\">评论</h3><p data-pid=\"heAnIKf-\">Roediger, H. L., &amp; Karpicke, J. D. (2018). Reflections on the Resurgence of Interest in the Testing Effect. Perspectives on Psychological Science, 13(2), 236–241. <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1177/1745691617718873\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1177/1745691</span><span class=\"invisible\">617718873</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a></p><h3 id=\"sec-6\">一手研究</h3><p data-pid=\"pERXLYwL\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Kang,_S._H._K.,_McDermott,_K._B.,_&amp;_Roediger,_H._L._(2007)._Test_format_and_corrective_feedback_modify_the_effect_of_testing_on_long-term_retention._European_Journal_of_Cognitive_Psychology,_19(4–5),_528–558._https\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Butler, A. (2010). Repeated Testing Produces Superior Transfer of Learning Relative to Repeated Studying. Journal of Experimental Psychology. Learning, Memory, and Cognition, 36, 1118–1133.</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup></p><p data-pid=\"0plrUUSV\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Kang,_S._H._K.,_McDermott,_K._B.,_&amp;_Roediger,_H._L._(2007)._Test_format_and_corrective_feedback_modify_the_effect_of_testing_on_long-term_retention._European_Journal_of_Cognitive_Psychology,_19(4–5),_528–558._https:\\/\\/doi.org\\/10.1080\\/09541440601056620\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Kang, S. H. K., McDermott, K. B., &amp; Roediger, H. L. (2007). Test format and corrective feedback modify the effect of testing on long-term retention. European Journal of Cognitive Psychology, 19(4–5), 528–558. HTTPS://doi.org/10.1080/09541440601056620</a></p><p data-pid=\"P1Ub2Kzm\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z78CeJK6CpQWhzruLZZ8cVxeQ2WaHgzHNmHsq\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Blunt, J. R. (2011). Retrieval Practice Produces More Learning than Elaborative Studying with Concept Mapping. Science, 331(6018), 772–775.</a></p><p data-pid=\"tp0nVmAC\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Karpicke,_J._D.,_&amp;_Smith,_M._A._(2012)._Separate_mnemonic_effects_of_retrieval_practice_and_elaborative_encoding._Journal_of_Memory_and_Language,_67(1),_17–29._https:\\/\\/doi.org\\/10.1016\\/j.jml.2012.02.004\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Smith, M. A. (2012). Separate mnemonic effects of retrieval practice and elaborative encoding. Journal of Memory and Language, 67(1), 17–29. HTTPS://doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2012.02.004</a></p><p data-pid=\"_bN536w3\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zRY97sYVywAXpocmqGiv6aL6TM7aA6ZK49Y2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Rohrer, D., Dedrick, R. F., Hartwig, M. K., &amp; Cheung, C.-N. (2020). A randomized controlled trial of interleaved mathematics practice. Journal of Educational Psychology, 112(1), 40–52.</a></p><p data-pid=\"mcj5FFAX\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2eKrnHvSL48vZ5zffUuxr5Xpp8GAEAt77iQ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Agarwal, P. (2019). Retrieval Practice &amp; Bloom’s Taxonomy: Do Students Need Fact Knowledge Before Higher Order Learning? Journal of Educational Psychology, 111, 189–209</a></p><h2 id=\"sec-7\">反向链接</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"ndS-LDwe\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"vpYn9wX9\">间隔重复记忆系统结合了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5oCe7JTrkYfmb6SHE4n5HxisE7PdwS6nmXEw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>，能够高效地记忆成千上万事实类的知识（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5rVJfPsyCU3pHBbhwef9DNR5fohTHCQFJWir\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统非常高效</a>）<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup>。有些人还扩展了它的用途（见下文）。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4bR1HVvDUhMXDm5SJB4Tiw4xGbrm9AfXWgbc\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-10\"><a href=\"#ref-10\">[10]</a></sup>，但它们不只仅用于背诵事实：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-11\"><a href=\"#ref-11\">[11]</a></sup>。</li></ul></ul><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><ul><li data-pid=\"6yQ-dXcc\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-11\"><a href=\"#ref-11\">[11]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"KlLl9dSc\">值得注意的是，间隔重复的认知心理学基础（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>）已被证明适用于概念性知识和陈述性知识（见 Karpicke 和 Blunt，2011）。<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"YeWk4WLn\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"47lAmg7B\">这种效应有时被等同于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>：当学生被要求从记忆中提取答案时（如在自由回忆测试中），对回忆质量的影响可部分归因于生成答案的过程。但 Karpicke 和 Zaromb(2010) 的实验表明，这两种影响是不同的，而且在一定程度上可能是彼此独立的。通过尝试生成目标来学习的人，最终比通过尝试回忆来学习的人回忆质量更差。</li></ul></ul><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><ul><li data-pid=\"Y_TlGVHq\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6yfTwYekzvBkVjeH7WBUrSAJhyGTMYDAyYW7\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记的维护近似于间隔重复</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-12\"><a href=\"#ref-12\">[12]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"aPTdXRl-\">从记忆的角度来说，这并不是一个有效的间隔重复：你并没有真正利用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>。但它确实利用了类似于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a>的东西，而且它可能是一个有用的视角，来思考如何在你长期积累的思想库中管理你的注意力。具体来说，这种做法将鼓励你反复关注那些似乎与你现在的工作有关的过去的想法。因为你可能会发现自己正在修改关于这些过去想法的笔记，所以这种关注可能是需要相当努力的。<br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"1oFb7-QG\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z88ihqREJVzHg3iwR7cRee4ZNevQvDYSzj7Zw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Nate Kornell</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"ZiNqho2x\">威廉姆斯学院的认知心理学教授，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zcHyJy8EutFjUfJcEUw7sYLJ4UVTmR3NDsYS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Robert A. Bjork</a> 的学生。他围绕<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5oCe7JTrkYfmb6SHE4n5HxisE7PdwS6nmXEw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应</a>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>进行了大量研究。</li></ul><li data-pid=\"oVj7qu2C\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7XLLk9aqBtJLDtP9kemBA87bDtjhpxst1osT\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆卡片应确保复习者必须从记忆中提取出答案</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-13\"><a href=\"#ref-13\">[13]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"35BMbhGY\">一个<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a>取决于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>：如果你必须从记忆中实际提取某样东西，你会比简单地重新接触它记得更久。因此，在写卡片时，要确保卡片要求读者实际提取出你想强化的记忆。</li></ul></ul><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><ul><li data-pid=\"mSLrLPYO\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5opHsGrNmCib7YQfLv6XbYURzZgZmx4Mrh5y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">§认真对待知识工作（Stripe 融合讲座，2019-12-12）</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"LI6shZxQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"-Aod-6_V\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8G4myETPfwXBLoBzHydJp36ArdD9oyedZdzM\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Jeffrey Karpicke</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"DqL9Bv_9\">实验认知心理学家，经常研究<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>。曾与 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2jatEERyjJtRQstvZnPUxC1uE1JUU8rAHAV\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Henry L. Roediger</a> 合作。<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"QsWOj3D7\"> [[Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Blunt, J. R. (2011). 提取练习产生的学习效果比用概念图进行的精细学习要好。Science, 331(6018), 772-775. <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1126/science.1199327\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1126/science</span><span class=\"invisible\">.1199327</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/><br/>* 实验比较了概念图（调用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>）与提取练习（调用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>）对记忆的影响。与 Karpicke 和 Smith(2012) 一样，本文也对提取练习的效果是否似乎是<b>由于</b>精细编码，或者是否有其他过程发生感兴趣。<br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"KR_xzY3a\"> [[Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Smith, M. A. (2012). 提取练习和精细编码的单独记忆效果。Journal of Memory and Language, 67(1), 17-29. <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2012.02.004\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2</span><span class=\"invisible\">012.02.004</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/><br/>* <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>是由<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>产生的吗？当你在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a>中复习卡片时，你给自己一个机会，根据你当前的背景和复习过程中的不同想法形成新的联系。<br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"jgIGNm6Z\"> [[Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Zaromb, F. M. (2010). 提取模式区分了测试效应和生成效应。Journal of Memory and Language, 62(3), 227-239. <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2009.11.010\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2</span><span class=\"invisible\">009.11.010</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/><br/>* <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a>是同一回事吗？它们经常被等同起来，事实上，我在自己的笔记中也曾将它们等同起来。本文描述了一系列的实验，试图证明有不同的基本机制在驱动这两种现象，而且提取练习对记忆的影响比生成更大。<br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"zNueYl94\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Log\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">筹备 2020 年 FOO 营会谈</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"ScV-VmbH\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"roBypnmA\"> [[Roediger, H. L., &amp; Karpicke, J. D. (2006). 测试记忆的力量：基础研究和对教育实践的影响。Perspectives on Psychological Science, 1(3), 181-210. <a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1111/j.1745-6916.2006.00012.x\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1111/j.1745-</span><span class=\"invisible\">6916.2006.00012.x</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/><br/>* 关于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>的详尽综述论文。这篇论文涵盖了在实验室环境和更实际的课堂环境中对测试的实验历史，并回顾了作者的一些最新研究。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2jatEERyjJtRQstvZnPUxC1uE1JUU8rAHAV\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Henry L. Roediger</a><br/> <br/></li><li data-pid=\"lLc0q2QZ\"> [[Rohrer, D., Dedrick, R. F., Hartwig, M. K., &amp; Cheung, C.-N.(2020). 穿插式数学练习的随机对照试验。<a class=\"external\" href=\"HTTPS://doi.org/10.1037/edu0000367\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">HTTPS://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1037/edu0000</span><span class=\"invisible\">367</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/><br/>* 穿插练习为<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5oCe7JTrkYfmb6SHE4n5HxisE7PdwS6nmXEw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应</a>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a>创造了一个自然环境。<br/> </li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-8\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"ow2WGDGE\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">间隔重复记忆系统（Spaced repetition memory system）</a></li><li data-pid=\"HiJ_Hkdi\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"536670074\" href=\"#/post/536670074\">提取练习和迁移学习</a></li><li data-pid=\"21ZWN4jL\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"455748242\" href=\"#/post/455748242\">生成效应</a></li><li data-pid=\"k1JRa7-j\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677785901\" href=\"#/post/677785901\">附加问题</a></li><li data-pid=\"VbLVvNMy\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677786021\" href=\"#/post/677786021\">附加问题能够提高学习者对相关但未直接测试的内容的理解</a></li><li data-pid=\"_YgB54Xv\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"719498216\" href=\"#/post/719498216\">程序教学</a></li><li data-pid=\"RoJfxDDt\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1660865898\" href=\"#/post/1660865898\">以想法为中心的记忆系统</a></li><li data-pid=\"wMQWJLl-\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1915475356250514194\" href=\"#/post/1915475356250514194\">解题示例效应</a></li><li data-pid=\"0QffpgHt\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1928197807031968828\" href=\"#/post/1928197807031968828\">某些活动（如弹钢琴、烹饪）为有针对性的练习提供了情境化的场所</a></li><li data-pid=\"a0eRXwKO\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1928747840647168044\" href=\"#/post/1928747840647168044\">提取练习</a></li><li data-pid=\"Nxp5nBGx\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1930200421491803500\" href=\"#/post/1930200421491803500\">绘制概念图</a></li><li data-pid=\"p0dqS_G3\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1939369330392409518\" href=\"#/post/1939369330392409518\">van Gog &amp; Sweller (2015)：《并非新论，却几近被遗忘：当学习材料复杂性增加时，测试效应随之减弱乃至消失》</a></li><li data-pid=\"jrWSL43s\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1939372515479749757\" href=\"#/post/1939372515479749757\">Yeo &amp; Fazio (2019)：《最佳学习策略取决于学习目标和过程：提取练习与解题示例之比较》</a></li><li data-pid=\"4FMxErJ_\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1939371849566909842\" href=\"#/post/1939371849566909842\">Chen, O., Castro-Alonso, J. C., Paas, F., &amp; Sweller, J. (2018)：《高元素交互性材料学习中的不合意困难效应》</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-9\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"5wzqzpei\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"b4Udd1zL\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Testing effect</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> Bjork ：「上帝啊，这个困难正合我意」—— 合意困难 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"490699755\" href=\"#/post/490699755\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 精细编码 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"458013236\" href=\"#/post/458013236\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 生成效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"455748242\" href=\"#/post/455748242\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 提取练习和迁移学习 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"536670074\" href=\"#/post/536670074\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 高效学习的间隔重复 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"420105707\" href=\"#/post/420105707\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 相较于重复学习，重复测试的迁移学习效果更好 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"604132912\" href=\"#/post/604132912\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 间隔效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"424603970\" href=\"#/post/424603970\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统非常高效 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"520108661\" href=\"#/post/520108661\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-10\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-10\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397582470\" href=\"#/post/397582470\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-11\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-11\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"398045447\" href=\"#/post/398045447\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-12\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-12\">↩</a> 常青笔记的维护近似于间隔重复 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"437448252\" href=\"#/post/437448252\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-13\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-13\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆卡片应确保复习者必须从记忆中提取出答案 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"402705173\" href=\"#/post/402705173\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"422370272","title":"发展技能需要挑战稳态","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":11,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"424603970","title":"间隔效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":18,"minutes":11,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"420105707","title":"(1/5) 高效学习的间隔重复——概述","author":"Gwern Branwen","votes":310,"minutes":10,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"490699755","title":"Bjork ：「上帝啊，这个困难正合我意」—— 合意困难","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":30,"minutes":6,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"1939371849566909842","title":"Chen, O., Castro-Alonso, J. C., Paas, F., & Sweller, J. (2018)：《高